# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# Without this, `docker build .` streams the whole repository to the daemon —
# 450 MB of node_modules the image reinstalls anyway, plus the design artifacts
# and the docs. It is slow, and it is how a `.env` ends up in an image layer.
#
# The paths are anchored rather than globbed: `**/dist` would also match
# `node_modules/@prisma/engines/dist`, which is where Prisma's downloaded query
# engine lives.

node_modules
**/node_modules
/dist
/apps/*/dist
/packages/*/dist
/apps/*/build
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets. Belt and braces: these are gitignored too, but a build context is
# not a git checkout and a developer's working tree may hold one.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Local state a container must never inherit.
.storage
.mail
*.log

# Not needed to run the API.
.git
.github
docs
design
infra

# The web app's source is not needed to run the API, but its manifest is: the
# lockfile describes the whole workspace, and `npm ci` refuses to install
# against a lockfile whose workspaces it cannot see.
apps/web/src
apps/web/public
apps/web/index.html

# Generated at build time from the schema, so a stale copy cannot ship.
apps/api/src/generated
